# LeakSanitizer suppressions for fontconfig's process-lifetime global caches.
#
# fontconfig deliberately keeps matched patterns (and its expat-parsed font
# config) alive for the whole process, so every run "leaks" a few hundred
# bytes that ASan flags even though the UI library itself is leak-free. The
# cui entry frame is Application() -> Painter::resolveTypeface ->
# FcFontMatch; suppress only below fontconfig's own Fc*/expat symbols so real
# leaks in cui code still surface.
#
# Usage: LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<path>/lsan_fontconfig.supp ./asan_test
leak:FcConfigParseAndLoadFromMemoryInternal
leak:FcConfigValues
leak:FcInitLoadOwnConfig
leak:FcPatternObject*
leak:FcValueList*
